## Design Rationale Summary:

| Task | Rule Type | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| find mountains | position_inside_box | Navigation task — player must walk from grass spawn into the stony_peaks zone (x≥8). Box covers the entire forced biome area. |
| mine gray_concrete | inventory_has | Mine task — mined block drops as item into inventory. Iron pickaxe provided. |
| craft to glass_pane | inventory_has | Craft task — crafted item ends up in inventory. Materials (6 glass) and crafting table provided. |
| find oak_pressure_plate | position_near_with_facing | Find/observe task — player must navigate near the pressure plate AND face it, confirming visual discovery. Target at (+10, 0, 0), within 5 blocks, facing within 60°. |

**Note on "find mountains"**: Since the evaluator doesn't have a native biome-check rule type, I use `position_inside_box` covering the area where `/fillbiome` forced stony_peaks. Entering this box means the player has navigated into the mountains zone. The box (x: 8-20, y: -5 to 10, z: -5 to 15) is generous and covers the entire forced biome area where all objectives are located.
